# Written for rpi-image-gen layer mp-hmi-usb.
#
# A USB stick at the panel, for the job list of the printer's interface: a
# filesystem on a USB disk is mounted read-only by mp-hmi-usb-mount@<name>,
# which the removal of the device stops. Only FAT and exFAT, the formats a
# stick comes in: every other filesystem is a kernel parser more that a
# prepared stick could aim at. The panel's own drive is NVMe and never
# matches. After 60-persistent-storage.rules, which reads the filesystem type.
ACTION!="remove", SUBSYSTEM=="block", SUBSYSTEMS=="usb", ENV{ID_FS_USAGE}=="filesystem", ENV{ID_FS_TYPE}=="vfat|exfat", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="mp-hmi-usb-mount@%k.service"
